join steak left
audio music "res://Soundtracks/Sir_Loin_song.mp3" [volume="-5.0"]
Howdy there, partner!
- What's your name?
	character: Um, Hi! What’s your name?
	steak: Name’s Loin, Fastest gunslinger in the west. Ma' full name is Sir Loin but my partners all said that sounded more like a knight, so it’s just Loin now. YEE HAW.
- Steak?
	character: You're a steak?
	steak: Yep! You know it partner! Fastest gunslinger in the west!
character: Right yea I see that.
character: [i] The west? What the hell does that mean?
steak: What sorta stuff ya into?
character: Erm.. I cook.
steak: Oh, that’s great! What are you making right now?
character: ...
character: ..You.
steak: Ah! How could I have stumbled on that one?
if {Entreevar} == "Brock":
	character: It’s fine!... It’s not like I was expecting you to be like that big buff gymbro.
	steak: I got some sand in me too! Hah!
else:
	character: It’s fine! It’s not like I was expecting you to be like that emotionless deadpan.
	steak: I will devote myself to be as delightful as I can be. Just like an Ace-High roller!
character: Why do you keep speaking like that?
steak: Like what? You startling my grooves.
character: Like THAT.
steak: Ah, you mean my superior way of speaking.
character: I…
steak: Well, if ya’ don’t mind me asking, I got a strong gut feeling that you ain’t from around these parts, are ya?
character: Actually I am. This is where I work. My job.
steak: Right! Shucks, pardon me, I must still be a bit shook from… y’know, comin’ into existence.
character: Yeah, that’s fine.
steak: …
character: So, uh…
- Dislike accent
	character: That way of speaking. It's kinda weird?
	steak: Oh, I’m doggone sorry. It’s just that from where I come from, it's normal to holler like this. Plus, I think it’s pretty solid.
	character: Yeah, right… I don’t want to be rude or anything, but it’s kind of bugging me.
	steak: You don’t like this way of speaking?!
	jump steakCOMFORT/
- Compliment accent
	character: The accent, I think it’s pretty neat.
	steak: Oh, well that’s just heartwarmin’. Cheers, partner!
	character: It’s all good.
	steak: I can teach ya’ if you want!
	jump steakTEACHING/
- Western movies
	character: What about those western movies?
	steak: Yea, you bet!
	character: So, what’s your favourite western?
	steak: I’d say… that good old western called, “The Unbeatable, the Unhealthy, and the Unsightly.”
	jump steakMOVIE/